    "video": "",
    "story": "A city that makes you earn every view. We walked roughly twelve kilometres a day, most of it vertical, and ate it all back in custard tarts.\n\nAlfama is the postcard, and it deserves to be, but the evening we remember was in **Graça** — a miradouro, a bottle of vinho verde bought from a kiosk, and a man playing fado to about nine people who all seemed to know him.",
    "recs": [
      {
        "kind": "eat",
        "name": "Cervejaria Ramiro",
        "note": "Shellfish by weight, beer by the litre. Expect to queue; it's worth it. Finish with the steak sandwich.",
        "url": ""
      },
      {
        "kind": "drink",
        "name": "Miradouro da Senhora do Monte",
        "note": "Highest viewpoint in the city, least crowded. Bring your own bottle.",
        "url": ""
      },
      {
        "kind": "do",
        "name": "Tram 28, but backwards",
        "note": "Ride it from the far end at Martim Moniz to get a seat, or skip it and walk the route.",
        "url": ""
      },
      {
        "kind": "tip",
        "name": "Shoes with grip",
        "note": "The pavement is polished limestone. In rain it's an ice rink and that is not a joke.",
        "url": ""
      }
    ]
  },
